      {
        "id": "p57-q28-part-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find all the points of inflection.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-\\pi,-\\pi)$, $(0,0)$ and $(\\pi,\\pi)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}-\\sin x&=0\\\\x&=-\\pi,\\ 0,\\ \\pi\\qquad(-2\\pi<x<2\\pi).\\end{aligned}$$\nThe signs of $y''$ on the successive intervals $(-2\\pi,-\\pi)$, $(-\\pi,0)$, $(0,\\pi)$ and $(\\pi,2\\pi)$ are $-$, $+$, $-$ and $+$. Thus concavity changes at each candidate.\n$$\\begin{aligned}y(-\\pi)&=-\\pi\\\\y(0)&=0\\\\y(\\pi)&=\\pi.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe points of inflection are $(-\\pi,-\\pi)$, $(0,0)$ and $(\\pi,\\pi)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q28-part-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Hence sketch the curve, for $-2\\pi\\le x\\le2\\pi$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Increasing through $(-2\\pi,-2\\pi)$, $(-\\pi,-\\pi)$, $(0,0)$, $(\\pi,\\pi)$ and $(2\\pi,2\\pi)$, with horizontal points of inflection at $(\\pm\\pi,\\pm\\pi)$.",
          "worked": "The function is odd, so the graph has rotational symmetry about the origin. It is increasing throughout the domain, with horizontal tangents at $(-\\pi,-\\pi)$ and $(\\pi,\\pi)$. Use the concavity changes from part c and include the endpoints $(-2\\pi,-2\\pi)$ and $(2\\pi,2\\pi)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
